---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
import Brief from '../../components/doc/Brief.astro';
import Closing from '../../components/Closing.astro';
import { COMPARES } from '../../data/compare';
import { siteBase } from '../../lib/site';
import { breadcrumb } from '../../lib/schema';

const SITE = siteBase(Astro.site);
const title = 'AdBoost Health vs. Agencies, In-House & DTC Shops';
const description = 'How a health-specialist paid-acquisition partner compares to a full-service healthcare agency, an in-house team, or a generalist DTC agency.';
const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumb(SITE, [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Compare', href: '/compare/' }]),
  {
    '@type': 'CollectionPage',
    name: 'AdBoost Health compared to the alternatives',
    url: `${SITE}/compare/`,
    hasPart: COMPARES.map((c) => ({ '@type': 'WebPage', name: c.h1, url: `${SITE}/compare/${c.slug}/` })),
    mainEntity: {
      '@type': 'ItemList',
      itemListElement: COMPARES.map((c, i) => ({ '@type': 'ListItem', position: i + 1, name: c.h1, url: `${SITE}/compare/${c.slug}/` })),
    },
  },
];
const arrow = '<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4"/></svg>';
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} canonicalPath="/compare/" {jsonLd}>
  <PageHead
    label="Compare"
    title="Weighing your *options?*"
    lede="An honest look at how a health-specialist acquisition partner compares to the alternatives, including when the alternative is the better call."
    dots
  />

  <section class="tone-paper page-body" data-nav="paper" aria-label="The comparisons">
    <div class="wrap cmp">
      <Brief>A health-specialist paid-acquisition partner like AdBoost Health is usually the better fit than a full-service healthcare agency, an in-house team, or a generalist DTC shop when growth is bottlenecked by ad-platform compliance and CAC, because it pairs health-vertical policy expertise with performance media in one team. A full-service agency wins when you need brand, PR, and web under one roof; an in-house team wins at large, stable spend where dedicated headcount pays for itself; a generalist DTC agency can be cheaper when your category carries no compliance risk. The three breakdowns below go dimension by dimension.</Brief>

      <div class="rows">
        {COMPARES.map((c, i) => (
          <a class="row" href={`/compare/${c.slug}/`} data-reveal="side">
            <span class="idx">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <span class="row-name">{c.h1}</span>
            <span class="row-arrow row-meta" set:html={arrow} />
            <span class="row-text small">{c.intent}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="doc-sec">
        <h2>How to read these comparisons</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Each breakdown is written at the category level and kept honest: it names where the alternative is genuinely the better choice, not just where we win. The deciding factors are almost always the same three. First, compliance risk: regulated health, telehealth, GLP-1, and supplement brands live or die by ad-platform policy, which is where a <a href="/advertising/">health-specialist</a> earns its keep. Second, stage and spend: a dedicated in-house team pays off at large, stable budgets, while an agency de-risks the ramp. Third, scope: if you need brand, PR, and a website rebuild alongside media, a full-service shop consolidates that, whereas if the bottleneck is <a href="/glossary/cac/">CAC</a> and rejected ads, that is the specialist lane. See real outcomes by <a href="/industries/telehealth/">vertical</a>, or start with the <a href="/services/">services</a> that drive them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Closing />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .cmp { display: grid; gap: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px); }
</style>
